ing behind the last index, especially for indexes that are persisted but\n../agent-source/api.go:1241:// the last index that was sent to the application's FSM over the apply channel\n../agent-source/api.go:1251:// stop accepting client requests, make sure the target server is up to date\n../agent-source/state.go:157:// getLastIndex returns the last index in stable storage.\n../agent-source/state.go:165:// getLastEntry returns the last index and term in stable storage.\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1012:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"bad last index: %d, expecting %d\", last, snap.Index)\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1088:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"bad last index: %d, expecting %d\", last, snap.Index)\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1163:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"bad last index: %d, expecting %d\", last, snap.Index)\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1485:\t// Get the last index before the restore.\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1517:\t\t// restoring onto a new cluster should always have a last index based\n../agent-source/raft_test.go:1530:\t// When first index is set to the next commit index / last index, then\n../agent-source/fsm.go:210:\t\t// Update the last index and term\n../agent-source/replication.go:200:// given last index.\n../agent-source/replication.go:201:// If the follower log is behind, we take care to bring them up to date.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
