{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > vote_candidate.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']))\n# Replace the answered verification accounting question at this related handoff.\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='b-verify':b['unknowns']=['Which legal timing histories make a false verification success externally stale despite independent lease checks?']\n if b['id']=='b-election':b['unknowns']=['Whether the vote tuple retains one coherent term/candidate meaning after partial stable-store failure; b-vote-persist and b-vote-receive expose the read paths.']\nm['core_overview']['open_details'][0]='Nonvoter responses contribute to verification support under the existing all-peer notification mechanism; externally stale-read consequences under autonomous lease/election timing remain open.'\nm['behaviors'].extend([\n dict(id='b-vote-persist',primary_activity='A6',execution_owner='Main-loop vote handler or candidate election',protocol_context='One attempted persistent term/candidate vote',trigger='requestVote or electSelf calls persistVote',writes=['LastVoteTerm then LastVoteCand in separate StableStore calls'],durable_effects=['First write can succeed while the second returns error; the helper does not roll back the first write.'],external_effects=['Returns the first write error or the candidate write error; caller declines the attempted vote on failure.'],produces_fact_ids=['f-vote-record'],source_ids=['src-persist-context','src-stable-interface','src-vote-handler','src-election-producer'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'The resulting stored pair is later used as same-term prior-vote evidence, including the early duplicate-grant branch.'},unknowns=['Backend-specific error guarantees are not documented by the minimal StableStore interface.']),\n dict(id='b-vote-receive',primary_activity='A2',execution_owner='Raft main-loop requestVote handler',protocol_context='Request term, candidate address, stored vote tuple and local last entry',trigger='RequestVote RPC dispatch',implementation_guards=['Candidate membership/suffrage, known leader and term guards precede persistent vote lookup.','Matching stored term and candidate returns Granted before last-log freshness checks.','On a nonduplicate new vote, lower candidate last term or shorter same-term log rejects; persistence error returns ungranted.'],consumes_fact_ids=['f-vote-record'],source_ids=['src-vote-handler','src-vote-rpc-fields','src-rpc-dispatch'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'A grant contributes to a candidate election, which selects the owner of later replicated decisions.'},unknowns=['Does a candidate-key write error make the duplicate branch bypass an otherwise applicable log freshness condition in a fully sourced same-history execution?'])])\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='f-vote-record',meaning='The stable store contains a LastVoteTerm integer and LastVoteCand byte string, read together by the vote handler as its prior-vote record; the two keys are written separately and do not intrinsically assert completion of the same persistVote call.',identity={'node':'local stable store','record':'LastVoteTerm and LastVoteCand keys'},validity_context='Values most recently retained by separate successful writes, including a prefix of an errored persistVote attempt.',representation=['keyLastVoteTerm','keyLastVoteCand'],durability='StableStore persists each successful write; the interface exposes no multi-key transaction.',recovery='NewRaft restores currentTerm; requestVote reads these keys directly when processing later requests, including after restart.',source_ids=['src-stable-interface','src-persist-context','src-vote-handler','src-startup'],unknowns=['Which concrete durable backends expose the scoped fail-without-overwrite candidate write?']))\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='Raft.persistVote partial storage failure':\n  s.update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-vote-persist','b-vote-receive'],reason='A successful vote-term write followed by a candidate-key error can retain an older candidate; determine the applicable freshness duty and actual producer history for the duplicate grant.')\nq=dict(question='Can a partial persistVote failure cause requestVote to grant a candidate whose last-log term is below the local last-log term, although that candidate had no prior successful vote persistence in the requested term?',importance='A stale-log candidate grant can weaken election log-freshness protection and potentially authorize a leader without retained history. The exploration establishes only receiver behavior under constructed inputs, not a competing leader or committed-history loss.',source_ids=['src-stable-interface','src-persist-context','src-vote-handler','src-startup','src-vote-rpc-fields','src-rpc-dispatch','src-election-producer','src-campaign','src-append-consumer'],participants=['Receiving voter','Previous candidate','New candidate','StableStore'],objects=['LastVoteTerm','LastVoteCand','RequestVoteRequest','Local last log entry'],contexts=['Stable voter configuration','One successful vote-term write and one candidate-key Set error that leaves the old candidate unchanged','No disk corruption or rollback of successful writes'],event_paths=['Old candidate vote -> newer local log -> fresh candidate request -> partial persistVote failure -> old candidate request in new term -> duplicate grant before freshness checks'],activity_classes=['A2','A6'],behavior_ids=['b-vote-persist','b-vote-receive'],fact_ids=['f-vote-record'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-election':'The actual election producer supplies request term/candidate/log fields and consumes grants.','b-append':'AppendEntries can establish a newer local last-log term without overwriting a vote record from an earlier election.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['The failing candidate-write attempt itself is not granted.','Without failure, the completed new candidate record causes the previous candidate request to be rejected.','A true duplicate vote may legitimately use an earlier same-term decision; a missing local recheck alone is not a defect.','StableStore does not document detailed backend failure semantics; the injected no-write error is an explicit narrow fault premise.'],unknowns=['Complete an actual election/log-production prefix preserving previous candidate identity and a newer local log without rollback or invented leader authority.','Ground the log-freshness obligation specifically when no successful prior vote in this term exists and the stable backend returns an explicit no-write error.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Exploration 7f796a9a61834e4db0f75cf6ab7c50d7 observed the injected branch retain (term 4, candidate a) after a failed write for b, then grant a with last-log term 1 against local term 3. The control rejected a. This justifies source/history construction; it is not formal evidence and must not be relabeled retrospectively.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\n# All selected sources, including supporting behavior sources, remain explicit.\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids'] or b['id'] in q['supporting_behavior_ids']:q['source_ids']+=b['source_ids']\nq['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(q['source_ids']))\njson.dump(m,open('map-votes.json','w'),indent=2)\nchanges={}\nfor id in ['b-verify','core_overview']:\n changes[id]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['src-verify-start','src-verify-notify','src-verify-vote'],rationale='Remove the answered local eligibility premise and preserve independent stale-read consequences. The accepted review and execution in feedback supply the observation; map sources remain implementation Materials.',preserves='The verified obligation, its all-peer dependencies and its local count observation are unchanged; no principal Fact meaning or identity is altered.')\nchang